    title: "Will Spain's housing crisis lead to a snap election?",
    summary: "The BBC's Guy Hedgecoe is in Madrid, where a series of marches have been scheduled, after Spain's Congress rejected measures aimed at tackling the country's housing crisis.",
    preview: "Thousands of people are continuing protests across Spain, after Congress rejected a series of measures aimed at tackling the country's housing crisis. Lawmakers voted on two decree-laws presented by government in response to nationwide protests that followed the eviction of 87-year-old Maricarmen Abascal from her home. Abascal was evicted after she was unable to pay a rent increase by the company that owns her flat. The case triggered a broader movement across the country demanding affordable rentals, which have soared in recent years.",
    body: "Thousands of people are continuing protests across Spain, after Congress rejected a series of measures aimed at tackling the country's housing crisis.\n\nLawmakers voted on two decree-laws presented by government in response to nationwide protests that followed the eviction of 87-year-old Maricarmen Abascal from her home.\n\nAbascal was evicted after she was unable to pay a rent increase by the company that owns her flat. The case triggered a broader movement across the country demanding affordable rentals, which have soared in recent years.\n\nThe BBC's Guy Hedgecoe is at one of the protests in Madrid and looks at whether the government's defeat will lead to an early general election, which is not due until next summer.\n\nRelated topics\n\n- Affordable housingUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- SpainUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- MadridUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- EvictionUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- RentingUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.",
